{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1110685,"ns":0,"title":"Modular representation theory","extract":"In mathematics, modular representation theory is the part of representation theory that studies linear representations of finite groups over fields of positive characteristic. As well as having applications to group theory, modular representations arise naturally in other branches of mathematics, such as algebraic geometry, number theory and combinatorics.","description":"Representation theory of finite groups over fields of positive characteristic","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}